ence about \"The Federation of Conservative Students ... broken up by the Chairman of the Conservative Party, Norman Tebbit, after one of its members had accused previous former Prime Minister Harold Macmillan of war crimes...\" Not relevant.\n\nThus we lack direct citation for Thatcher being succeeded by Major. The question asks for a UK Prime Minister succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party. Could also be John Major succeeded by Tony Blair (Labour) in 1997, but Blair was not Conservative Party leader. So not.\n\nThus answer likely \"Margaret Thatcher\". But we need citation. We don't have citation confirming succession. Could we use evidence that John Major was Conservative Party leader after Thatcher? Not present. The evidence about 1997 leadership election says John Major resigned as leader after defeat. Not about Thatcher.\n\nWe might need to answer \"noanswer\" due to lack of supporting evidence. The instruction: verify claims against quoted evidence. If we cannot find evidence, answer noanswer.\n\nThus answer noanswer."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1775,"completion_tokens":612,"total_tokens":2387,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791982389,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}